  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nThe locate took mates on the part only. Thus a user could not seat the stock on a vise that was already placed. The fixture collision checks and the carried-workholding check then read a stock place that nobody set.\r\n\r\n- `fixture_locate`: `LocateSpec` has a new field `body` (`LocateBody::Part` is the default, `LocateBody::Stock` is new). `stock_of` finds the stock of the fixture's setup. With the stock held, the mates are on the stock, in the stock's own pose.\r\n- `LocatePart`: with the stock held, the part moves and the stock follows it (stock-follow law). The part keeps its place in the blank. The locate is one undo step.\r\n- Refusals by name: a stock locate with no part, a setup with no stock, a mate on the wrong body. A square stock re-fits round a turned part with the allowance of each setup side. If that re-fit leaves the stock faces off the mates, `stock_lands` refuses the locate (\"would not land on the mates\").\r\n- Review fix (head `32102879d`): `stock_lands` (now in `crates/app/src/fixture_locate_land.rs`) judges each picked stock face, not only the box of the stock. The face is placed where the mates put it. The followed stock must have facets that face the same way (`NORMAL_TOL` = 1e-4 on 1 - cos of the angle, about 0.8 degree) and lie on that plane (`LEN_TOL_MM` = 1e-4 mm). These facets must cover the face area (`FACE_AREA_REL_TOL` = 0.1 %) and each facet centre of the face. A picked stock vertex must be a corner of the followed stock. A failure is refused in `LocatePart::new`. The message names the stock face and the fixture face: \"mate N: <stock face> of the stock '<stock>' would stand across the plane of, not flat on, <fixture face> of '<fixture>' - ... locate it without a turn, or locate the part\".\r\n- MCP: `locate_part` takes `\"body\": \"stock\"` (the default is `\"part\"`). `list_features` lists the faces of a stock.\r\n- UI: the locate form shows \"Place by: Stock faces / Part faces\". It holds the stock by default when the fixture's setup has a stock. While the stock is held, the picks pass over the parts inside the stock, so a stock face round a part can be picked.\r\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2173-locate-stock-on-vise.md`.\r\n\r\n## Effect on checks and posted output\r\n\r\nNo change for existing projects and scripts: the API and MCP default stay `Part`. The new path moves the part and its stock as a part locate does. The existing locate tests pass unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n- `crates/app/tests/fixture_locate_stock_body.rs`:\r\n  - `the_stock_locates_on_an_existing_vise_and_undo_puts_it_back`\r\n  - `the_fixture_collision_check_reads_the_located_stock` (`fixture_clash::after_fixture_move` reads the located stock)\r\n  - `a_stock_that_would_miss_its_mates_is_refused_by_name`\r\n  - `the_part_stays_the_default_body`\r\n  - `mcp_locate_part_seats_the_stock_by_its_feature_ids`\r\n- `crates/app/tests/fixture_locate_stock_cylinder.rs` (review fix):\r\n  - `a_cylinder_cap_mated_across_its_plane_is_refused` (the review repro: D20 x H20 cylinder, cap on a +X stop face)\r\n  - `a_cylinder_cap_mated_on_the_floor_lands_at_the_right_height` (the legal twin; the collision check reads the landed stock)\r\n  - `a_turned_cylinder_cap_on_the_floor_is_judged_by_its_face_and_lands` (a re-fit with new facets goes through the face check)\r\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: `egui_app::locate_tests::the_fixtures_page_locates_the_stock_on_the_vise`\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\nReview fix, head `32102879d` (on the PR base, no merge of main):\r\n- `camcraft-app`: `fixture_locate` 11/11, `fixture_locate_stock` 3/3, `fixture_locate_stock_body` 5/5, `fixture_locate_stock_cylinder` 3/3, `fixture_plate_followups` 4/4, `mcp_setup` 9/9, `mcp_pick` 7/7, `mcp_lay_face` 1/1.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -j 6 -- -D warnings`: clean. The fix changes no UI code.\r\n- Mutation checks: `face_lands` always true makes `a_cylinder_cap_mated_across_its_plane_is_refused` fail. `face_lands` always false makes `a_turned_cylinder_cap_on_the_floor_is_judged_by_its_face_and_lands` fail. With the rigid-carry shortcut off, all the stock suites above still pass.\r\n\r\nFirst head `c492f7006`:\r\n\r\n- `camcraft-app`: `fixture_locate` 11/11, `fixture_locate_stock` 3/3, `fixture_locate_stock_body` 5/5, `fixture_plate_followups` 4/4, `mcp_setup` 9/9, `mcp_pick` 7/7, `mcp_lay_face` 1/1.\r\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: 933 pass, 1 fail. The fail is `stock_fit_controls_follow_the_selected_shape`; it also fails on main (#2170, fix in PR #2171).\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick` did not complete in 50 min on a busy machine (my `timeout` stopped it; no test failed). I ran its parts above one by one.\r\n- `one_pick_rule::locate_and_points_drafts_take_box_corners_as_points` now sets the body to Part. Its document has a stock, and the test pins the part corner.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- A stock locate in a setup with a turned frame (the tests use the default setup frame).\r\n- A cylinder stock with a turn that is not a multiple of the facet angle. The box check refuses it (the turned facets change the box). This refusal is safe, but a user can find it too strict.\r\n- A stock vertex mate after a re-fit (the vertex branch of the check has no test of its own).\r\n- The camcraft-ui suites after the review fix (the fix changes no UI code).\r\n- The GUI by hand (no screenshots).\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\nSame document in each image: a 100 x 60 x 10 mm vise, a 20 x 10 x 8 mm part away from it, and a box stock round the part. The Fixtures page is open and \"Locate part...\" is armed. The images come from the test harness render of the full window at 1440x960.\r\n\r\nBefore (main): the locate form has no \"Place by\" choice. It locates the part only.\r\n\r\n![before](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/6c283eb7820560d7a3a375c10227b2ae5763282c/pr-2184/before-locate-form.png?raw=true)\r\n\r\nAfter (this PR): the form has \"Place by: Stock faces / Part faces\". The title reads \"Locate the stock of part in vise\".\r\n\r\n![after form](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/6c283eb7820560d7a3a375c10227b2ae5763282c/pr-2184/after-locate-form.png?raw=true)\r\n\r\nAfter: the bottom face of the stock (mate 1) and the top face of the vise are picked. Both faces are drawn in the viewport.\r\n\r\n![after mates](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/6c283eb7820560d7a3a375c10227b2ae5763282c/pr-2184/after-mates-picked.png?raw=true)\r\n\r\nAfter: \"Apply locate\" ran. The stock bottom now sits on the vise top, and the part moved with the stock.\r\n\r\n![after seated](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/6c283eb7820560d7a3a375c10227b2ae5763282c/pr-2184/after-stock-seated.png?raw=true)\r\n\r\nChangelog: Fixtures: the locate can seat the stock on a placed vise (\"Place by: Stock faces\"); the part follows inside the stock. MCP `locate_part` takes `\"body\": \"stock\"`.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nFixes #2173\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n",
